817:     /**
818:      * Terminates a TaskManager with the given index.
819:      *
820:      * <p>See {@link #startTaskManager()} to understand how TaskManagers are indexed. This method
821:      * terminates a TaskManager with a given index but it does not clear the index. The index stays
822:      * occupied for the lifetime of the MiniCluster and its TaskManager stays terminated. The index
823:      * is not reused if more TaskManagers are started with {@link #startTaskManager()}.
824:      *
825:      * @param index index of the TaskManager to terminate
826:      * @return {@link CompletableFuture} of the given TaskManager termination
827:      */
828:     public CompletableFuture<Void> terminateTaskManager(int index) {
829:         synchronized (lock) {
830:             final TaskExecutor taskExecutor = taskManagers.get(index);
831:             return taskExecutor.closeAsync();
832:         }
833:     }
